(SECTION 2: COOLING SYSTEM DIAGNOSIS & BLEEDING) '
() '
(Engine Overheating Troubleshooting:) '
(1. Check coolant reserve tank level when cold. If below MIN line, inspect for leaks.) '
(2. If temperature gauge needle reaches H \(Hot\), turn off A/C and safely stop engine.) '
(3. Radiator Fan Operation: Ensure both radiator fan and condenser fan activate when) '
(   engine coolant temperature reaches 199 deg F \(93 deg C\).) '
(4. Bleeding Air from Cooling System: Fill reserve tank to MAX. Loosen bleed bolt if) '
(   equipped until coolant flows without air bubbles, then tighten to 7.2 lb-ft \(10 N-m\).) '
ET
endstream
endobj
